<title>ITALY: ENI stock opens up in Milan after sale.</title>
<headline>ENI stock opens up in Milan after sale.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Italy's state-controlled energy giant ENI opened 0.42 percent higher at 7,200 lire on the Milan stock exchange after its second tranche share sale, dealers said.</p>
<p>Last week's sale of some 14 percent of ENI stock, hailed by the government as a great success, raised about eight trillion lire for the Treasury.</p>
<p>At 1006 GMT, over one million ENI shares had changed hands on the Bourse which posted an overall gain of 0.34 percent.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129589</p>
</text>
